# FINAL CLARIFICATION — SIMPLIFY DRIVER ACCOUNT CREATION FLOW

Discard the previous staged-user / verify-before-create architecture.

Do NOT implement:

* staged User accounts
* `send-verification-otp` before Driver creation
* separate email verification before account creation
* temporary/incomplete User records
* special cleanup for staged Driver accounts
* Owner-specific verification APIs

Use the existing application's traditional account creation + email verification architecture.

The existing Customer signup/email verification flow should be the primary reference.

---

# 1. FINAL BUSINESS FLOW

The Owner creates the Driver account first.

Owner enters:

* Driver Name
* Mobile
* Email
* Initial Password
* License Number
* License Expiry Date
* License Front Image
* License Back Image
* Other Driver fields required by the existing SRS

Then Owner clicks:

```text
[ Create Driver ]
```

Backend creates the Driver account normally.

After successful account creation, the frontend redirects the Owner to the email verification UI.

Expected flow:

```text
OWNER
   |
   | Driver details
   | Email
   | Initial Password
   | License details/images
   |
   v
[ CREATE DRIVER ]
   |
   v
Driver Account Created
   |
   +--> emailVerified = false
   +--> approvalStatus = PENDING
   +--> DriverStatus = INACTIVE
   |
   v
Redirect to Email Verification UI
   |
   v
OTP sent to Driver Email
   |
   v
Enter OTP
   |
   v
Existing Common Auth Email Verification
   |
   v
emailVerified = true
   |
   v
Driver can login
```

