## FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The implementation is correct only if:

* Driver account is created normally first.
* DriverProfile is created during account creation.
* Email verification happens after account creation.
* Frontend redirects to email verification after successful Driver creation.
* Existing common Auth email verification is reused.
* No staged User architecture exists.
* No pre-creation verification API exists.
* Owner provides the initial password.
* Password is encoded using PasswordEncoder.
* No system-generated password exists.
* No credential email is sent.
* Owner manually communicates credentials.
* Driver can login after email verification.
* Pending Driver can login but cannot be assigned.
* Approved Driver becomes ACTIVE and assignable.
* Driver uses existing common Forgot Password / Reset Password.
* No Driver-specific authentication or OTP mechanism is created.
* Existing Customer signup/email verification remains unaffected.

Implement only the minimum changes required for this final flow.
